[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix. The reports say otherwise. Dates go wrong for
**three different reasons**, and the queued fix covers one of them.

<Callout>
Not one known issue. Three problems, each with its own ticket.
</Callout>

## The three problems

<SplitTable ticket={4471} />

| ticket | problem | what happens |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [#1](https://github.com/nifesimii/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/1) | `parser` | The shared parser reads every date month first. A day-first tenant's dates come out flipped. |
| [#2](https://github.com/nifesimii/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/2) | `hint` | booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. Day-first tenants type what it says, and the form reads it day first. |
| [#3](https://github.com/nifesimii/mega-s01e03-4471/issues/3) | `one-day` | The date is one day off. The month and the day are not swapped. |

The numbers above are computed from the export, not typed.

## How we told them apart

A report's cause depends on its tenant: the locale it writes dates in, and the booking form it
runs. The intake tag is a guess from the reporter's browser. The table shows how
far it is off: intake tagged some `parser` reports `hint`, and some `hint` reports `parser`.

The one-day reports come from the desk's own notes (`oneDayMove` in `desk-notes.json`). Read them:
"Tuesday 12 May. Calendar says Monday 11 May", "Every booking in June is one day off", "Client in
Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday". None of them swaps a month and a day. We think
they point at time zones. The export cannot prove it, so #3 asks someone to check.

## What the subject line hid

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. The table
counts the subject lines that appear under more than one problem: most of them do. A subject says how a person felt about
the bug. It does not say which bug it is. This is why three problems ended up as one ticket.

## What to do

- Fix the parser for day-first tenants. That is the queued fix, and it closes #1 only.
- Make booking-v3 show the order the tenant writes, or make the form read what the hint says. #2 stays open until one of them ships.
- Look at the one-day reports for a time zone cause (#3).
- Replace decision 0001 with a new record. Do not edit it: accepted records are never edited.
- Until then, do not merge a report on its subject line alone. Check the tenant and the channel.

## Check my work

- Four `parser` reports (R-41290, R-41417, R-41514, R-41615) do not name a date pair. They are filed under `parser` because of their tenant, as `causes.ts` says. Every other `parser` and `hint` report shows a clear month and day flip.
- The `hint` reports all come through the form channel, from three tenants: Alder Physio, Copper Studio and Pale Harbour.

